Yes, conjunctions in natural languages are not consistent or logical.  
This is not a surprise.

I found myself musing about what the emphases would be for the two 
different meanings... Here's what I said in #jbopre:

One is ??- / ??-? / ??-?.  would you LIKE cream or SUGar in your COFfee.
The other is ???- / ?-? / ??-?.  Would you like CREAM or SUGar in your 
COFfee.

(wrong Unicode symbols for the syllables, but they're easier to see)

Don't overemphasize the long syllables, and it works.  Really.  Yes, you 
*can* ask that question in the sense of "would you like ANYTHING" in 
your coffee.

~mark

